    "result_text": "All 23 tests pass and the build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment (`'<customerCode>-M<YY>'`, YY = last two digits of the `registrationDate` year) by following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **New step function** \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber.java`: reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes `customerCode + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`, and mutates the entity in place.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted `assignMembershipNumber` (governed by the same `transaction`) right after `assignCustomerCode` (so `customerCode` exists) and before `assignHousehold`/`save`.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added the `membershipNumber` field mapped to a `membership_number` column, with getter/setter.\n\n4. **Response DTO** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name into the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\n5. **Schema/seed data** \u2014 added the `membership_number` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and added the corresponding trailing `NULL` to the 10 column-less owner seed inserts in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the only data file using positional inserts) to keep the column count matched.\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes, and the full suite (23 tests) is green.",
